.TH  pssec  1 "2026/06/19"

.SH SYNOPSIS

.PP
pssec is a simple tool that displays some security features (or issues) active on running processes. It\(aqs intended to help decision making around process security. Currently it is aware of \(aqno new privs\(aq flag, seccomp, writable exectuable memory, raw sockets, network servers, and connections to remote hosts.
.SH USAGE

.nf
.ft CW
.RS
.EX

  pssec [OPTIONS]
.RE
.EE
.fi
.in
.ad b
.nop  
.SH OPTIONS

.PP
.in +2

.TP
.B -fdleak <num>
set maximum number of file descriptors above which we raise a 'fdleak' warning (default 200)

.TP
.B --fdleak <num>
set maximum number of file descriptors above which we raise a 'fdleak' warning (default 200)

.TP
.B -pdisplay <num>
limit of 'max pids' that we consider to be constrained, and thus display as a security limit (default 200)

.TP
.B -fdisplay <num>
limit of 'max open files' that we consider to be constrained, and thus display as a security limit (default 200)

.TP
.B -pid <pid>
display only requested pid

.TP
.B --pid <pid>
display only requested pid

.TP
.B -S
only show processes that are network servers

.TP
.B -servers
only show processes that are network servers

.TP
.B --servers
only show processes that are network servers

.TP
.B -P
only show processes that can escalate priviledge (su)

.TP
.B -priv
only show processes that can escalate priviledge (su)

.TP
.B --priv
only show processes that can escalate priviledge (su)

.TP
.B -R
only show processes with remote connections open

.TP
.B -remote
only show processes with remote connections open

.TP
.B --remote
only show processes with remote connections open

.TP
.B -M
only show processes with exectuable memory that is writable, executable stack, or exectuable heap

.TP
.B -mem
